---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Now from "@/components/Now.astro";
---

<Layout title="About - Pavel Kleisner">

    <section class="page-head with-avatar">
        <img class="avatar" src="/pavel.jpg" alt="Pavel Kleisner" width="300" height="300" />
        <div>
            <h1>About me</h1>
            <p class="sub">A calm, practical engineer who still genuinely enjoys making and fixing things.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <div class="book">
        <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
            <p>On this page</p>
            <a href="#background">Background</a>
            <a href="#how">How I work</a>
            <a href="#avoid">What I avoid</a>
            <a href="#offline">Offline</a>
        </nav>

        <div>
            <section class="chapter" id="background">
                <h2>Background</h2>
                <p>I've worked with DataLite since 2017 and grew there from junior through senior engineer to team lead. For the last several years I've been a self-employed contractor on their client projects. I'm at my best where correctness, compatibility and release safety matter, where the code meets domain rules, integration contracts and production.</p>
                <p>I expect from the people around me what I try to bring myself: real effort to get the work done and to keep learning.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="chapter" id="how">
                <h2>How I work</h2>
                <dl class="rows">
                    <div><dt>Small, explicit changes</dt><dd>In a live system a precisely named rule, an isolated mapping or one focused test usually beats a big rewrite.</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Modern when it pays off</dt><dd>New versions and tools when they make the system more reliable, more observable or easier to change. Not for the CV.</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Not done at deploy</dt><dd>The real system starts after deployment: old data, retries, external contracts, logs, metrics and whoever has to support it.</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>AI agents</dt><dd>They take as much of the work as they reasonably can. Reviewing it and deciding what ships is my job.</dd></div>
                </dl>
            </section>

            <section class="chapter" id="avoid">
                <h2><span class="badge b-boss">Nerfed</span> What I deliberately avoid</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li><b>Over-engineering.</b> The "flexible" abstraction is usually the code everyone is afraid to touch two years later.</li>
                    <li><b>Big-bang releases.</b> A rollout needs an order, a fallback and a way to stop halfway, otherwise it's a bet.</li>
                    <li><b>One-person architecture.</b> I've been that person. It doesn't scale and it ruins holidays.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section class="chapter" id="offline">
                <h2>Offline</h2>
                <p>From the Krkonoše foothills, living just outside Prague with my family. I read a lot, mostly audiobooks (LitRPG and Czech sci-fi), play games to switch off, listen to metal and grind my coffee by hand.</p>
                <div style="margin-top:1.2rem"><Now lang="en" /></div>
            </section>
        </div>
    </div>

    <section class="party">
        <div>
            <h2>Sounds like a good fit?</h2>
            <p>Email is the fastest way to reach me.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="mailto:contact@pavelkleisner.dev">contact@pavelkleisner.dev</a>
    </section>

</Layout>
